{
  "slug": "ai-instruct",
  "name": "Ai Instruct",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Five practical skills covering the domains developers most often Google when shipping a website. Each skill auto-loads only when relevant to the task: Web Accessibility on UI work, SEO/LLMO before launch, Core Web Vitals on performance issues, AWS SPA deploy on Amplify/CDK work, and Google Analytics 4 on tracking setup. Originally distributed as standalone markdown guides for any AI tool (also available via npx ai-instruct init); now packaged as a single Claude Code plugin for one-command install.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `aws-spa-deploy` (Use this skill whenever the user is deploying a React/Vite single-page app to AWS, or mentions Amplify, CDK,…), `google-analytics-4` (Use this skill whenever the user installs, configures, or debugs Google Analytics 4, or mentions gtag.js, GTM, conversion…), `seo-llmo` (Use this skill whenever the user is building, reviewing, or preparing to launch any public-facing website or web…), `web-accessibility` (Use this skill whenever the user is building or reviewing any web UI), `web-performance` (Use this skill whenever the user is improving Core Web Vitals or page load performance, or mentions slow…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ai-instruct@claude-community` from `ziniman/ai-instruct`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
